  The application packets for the Fiscal Year 2013-2014 CDBG grant cycle were
distributed to all of the agencies who attended the training session.  A copy of the
Sub-Grantee Procedures was also handed out and explained.  15 individuals
attended this training.  For those agencies who could not attend the training session
the application was mailed at their request.  Several agencies also requested that the
application be e-mailed to them at their place of business.  The application deadline
was set as October 23, 2012.

  A Public Notice was published and a news release was sent out inviting city
residents to a Public Hearing on Wednesday, November 7, 2012.  A PowerPoint
presentation showed what the anticipated funding for Fiscal Year 2013-2014 was
going to be, along with the applications that were received.  The tentative
entitlement allocation was identified as $375,173 and $259,564 is anticipated for
recaptured funds.  Program Administration (anticipated $75,034) are the funds
utilized for the Housing and Community Development Office daily operations and
administration of programs.  Program Administration is taken off the top of the CDBG
Entitlement Allocation.  Seven Public Service applications totaling $143,650 were
received which is 282% greater than the $55,000 available.  Twelve General Service
applications totaling $2,279,905 were received which is 435% greater than the funds
available.  Ten individuals attended the Public Hearing.  No written comments were
received.

  The funding requests received and the professionalism of the grant proposals for
Fiscal Year 2013-2014 demonstrated the need within the community and the
competitiveness of the City’s Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) Program.

  Four Public Service applicants and nine General Service applicants were requested
to present the H&CD Office with a full application package.  The H&CD Office also
requested that one of their projects proceed to the next phase.  The application
deadline was December 19, 2012.  Upon receipt the applications were reviewed by
the H&CD Office to ensure all documents were received.  All grant proposals received
